Content:
@tnt phase noise future when [probably not this week]....? https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SOHjFtw0sgo .... for the frequencies you're dealing with, I think a pair of RTL-SDR's should actually be able to do it?
I'm guessing there's some gnuradio or mayhaps more-dedicated DSP bundle around that can do the mentioned carrier lock, carrier-surpression, cross-correlation steps.
Not gonna do _too well,_ but I can't expect that ASIC VCO to be hard-to-measure levels of low-phase-noise.
